-- title:
--   Compact sets are covered by finitely many translates of a neighbourhood of zero
-- statement:
--   Let $A\subseteq\mathbb R^\iota$ be compact for a finite index set $\iota$, and let $B$ be a neighbourhood of $0$. Then finitely many translates of $B$ cover $A$: there are $c_1,\dots,c_M$ with
--   $$
--   A\subseteq\bigcup_{j\le M}(c_j+B).
--   $$
--
--   This guarantees that the covering numbers of the construction are genuine minima of nonempty sets.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/openai/math/blob/1581d4cbdd69a0faf34b2089614fe2a814316a6a/lean/OAI/Analysis/MetricEntropy/CoveringNumber.lean#L102-L119

